let of 2s. The triplet of 2s can later be used to carry the small 6 (as a triplet with attached card), leaving me with strong pairs and high cards. Passing here would be passive given I have a "useless" single 10 that fits perfectly over the 7.\n\nReason: The 10 is the lowest single card that beats the 7. It preserves the pairs (KK) and triplet (222) for later control. It helps clear one of the four singles in hand.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♣10"]}'}
